# A BallVector with 2-limb centers times a number a of T that the program supplies (milestone2.md,
# "BallVector": bv_scale_k): bv_scale_2 with the step bv_scale_step_2, which guards a before mul_2_1
# takes it as a factor of its fused operations (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation:
# architecture.md). The centers by mul_2_1, entry by entry; the state that of norm_upper_2 on the
# centers written; the one radius bv_scale_radius_2 at the largest magnitude, the largest of the
# radii of ball_scale_2 entry by entry; norm_finish_1 tests that it is finite. When it is not (the
# operand is the whole space, a is not finite, or something overflowed), every center written is
# zero and the radius +infinity: the whole space. One addition more per entry: a fold has no line
# that guards a scalar once before its loop; and one per call in the radius, bv_scale_radius_entry_2,
# so that the loop is bv_scale_2 on the guarded a. Its claims are those of bv_scale_2.
fold:          bv_scale_2_entry
arrays:        stored x = x0 x1
scalars:       stored rx, supplied a
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = bv_scale_step_2(x, a)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_2(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_scale_radius_entry_2(m, rx, a)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z = z0 z1
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         x*a
requires:      ball_vector x rx
ensures:       encloses_entries z r x*a x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le((abs(x)+rx)*a,-2) radii_when=abs_le(rx*a,-2)
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/BvReal.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBv.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        mul_2_1 on the centers, a guarded (bv_scale_step_2), the radius of ball_scale_2 at the largest center (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
